pends on the remainder when \\(n\\) is divided by 4. We need to find the remainder when 53 is divided by 4:\n\n\\[\n53 \\div 4 = 13 \\text{ remainder } 1\n\\]\n\nSo, the remainder is 1, which means \\(7^{53}\\) has the same units digit as \\(7^1\\). Since the units digit of \\(7^1\\) is 7, the units digit of \\(7^{53}\\) is \\(\\boxed{7}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{7}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"number_theory:519"}
